/**
 * Fullstackverse + SkillVerse form backend — Google Apps Script Web App
 *
 * Receives every form on www.fullstackverse.in (via src/lib/appsScript.js),
 * writes each one to its own tab in the bound Google Sheet, emails the team
 * about new leads, and sends event confirmation emails.
 *
 * Requests (POST, JSON body sent as text/plain; field `action` picks the handler):
 *   submit_contact      Business enquiry dialog, RFP form, SkillVerse Quick Apply,
 *                       Campus Ambassador application (routed by `type`)
 *   submit_webinar      Webinar / workshop / course registrations (`webinar_slug`)
 *   send_webinar_email  Confirmation email for a registered event
 * Every request also carries `source` ("<page title> (<path>)").
 * Responses are always HTTP 200 JSON: { success: boolean, message?: string }.
 *
 * SETUP
 * 1. Open the Google Sheet that should receive submissions.
 * 2. Extensions > Apps Script (the script is bound to that sheet).
 * 3. Replace the editor contents with this file and save.
 * 4. Deploy > New deployment > Web app; Execute as: Me; Who has access: Anyone.
 * 5. Run testBusinessEnquiry once from the editor and approve the
 *    Sheets + Gmail permissions it asks for (the web app cannot ask visitors).
 * 6. Put the /exec URL in site_config.py (FORMS["apps_script_url"]) and the
 *    GitHub variable VITE_GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL.
 * A standalone script (created at script.google.com) also needs
 * FORMS["spreadsheet_id"] in site_config.py.
 * To update an existing deployment: Deploy > Manage deployments > edit >
 * Version: New version > Deploy (the URL stays the same).
 * Run the test* functions below from the editor to check each form type.
 */

